  "tagline": "Object-storage-backed distributed tracing backend with TraceQL search and trace-derived metrics.",
  "description": "Grafana Tempo is a high-volume tracing backend that writes spans as Parquet blocks to object storage and keeps only minimal indexes, which makes storing 100% of traces affordable. It ingests OpenTelemetry, Jaeger and Zipkin formats, and TraceQL lets you search spans by attributes, structure and duration and compute metrics from traces. Tempo 3.0 (May 2026) completed a move to a new ingest architecture that replaces legacy ingesters, made TraceQL metrics generally available and removed deprecated 2.x components, so upgrades need a migration. It pairs naturally with Grafana, Mimir and Loki.",
